window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-kouenji-rokusuke"]=[{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p20-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke bus priority seat debate  absolute egoism crowded bus on entrance morning  koenji sits with his legs crossed in the designated priority seating  well built athletic frame  blond hair  dressed in the anhs uniform  ignores the wobbling elderly woman standing near him  when kushida approaches and politely asks him to give up his seat  he smirks and rebuffs her without shifting an inch   why should i offer up my seat  there s no reason for me to do so   i don t understand  priority seats are just that  priority seats  i have no legal obligation to move  since i m currently occupying this seat  i should be the one who determines whether or not i move  am i supposed to give up my seat just because i m young  ha  that reasoning is nonsense  flashes a pointlessly vigorous smile  slides his earphones in  and begins listening to cacophonous music  his smug  self important attitude remains fixed as the office lady clenches her teeth   a contribution to society  you say  well  that is a rather interesting opinion  it s certainly true that offering up one s seat to the elderly could be viewed in such a positive light  unfortunately  i have no interest in contributing to society  i care only for my own satisfaction  oh  and one more thing  you re asking me  the one in the priority seat  to give up his spot  but couldn t you simply ask one of the other people seated on this crowded bus  if you truly cared for the elderly  then something like priority seating would be a rather trivial concern  wouldn t you agree  flawless aristocratic arrogance  unshakeable rationalized selfishness  completely immune to public shaming  peer pressure  or conventional morality  sharp philosophical debater who exposes the hypocrisy of the crowd  theatrical  high handed  grandiloquent aristocratic rhetoric  complete dismissal of her moral appeal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Bus priority seat debate: absolute egoism<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.20–22<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crowded bus on entrance morning. Kōenji sits with his legs crossed in the designated priority seating. Well-built athletic frame, blond hair, dressed in the ANHS uniform.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why should I offer up my seat? There’s no reason for me to do so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t understand. Priority seats are just that: priority seats. I have no legal obligation to move. Since I’m currently occupying this seat, I should be the one who determines whether or not I move. Am I supposed to give up my…”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“A contribution to society, you say? Well, that is a rather interesting opinion. It’s certainly true that offering up one’s seat to the elderly could be viewed in such a positive light. Unfortunately, I have no interest in…”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ignores the wobbling elderly woman standing near him. When Kushida approaches and politely asks him to give up his seat, he smirks and rebuffs her without shifting an inch.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t understand. Priority seats are just that: priority seats. I have no legal obligation to move. Since I’m currently occupying this seat, I should be the one who determines whether or not I move. Am I supposed to give up my seat just because I’m young? Ha! That reasoning is nonsense.”<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flashes a pointlessly vigorous smile, slides his earphones in, and begins listening to cacophonous music; his smug, self-important attitude remains fixed as the office lady clenches her teeth.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A contribution to society, you say? Well, that is a rather interesting opinion. It’s certainly true that offering up one’s seat to the elderly could be viewed in such a positive light. Unfortunately, I have no interest in contributing to society. I care only for my own satisfaction. Oh, and one more thing. You’re asking me, the one in the priority seat, to give up his spot, but couldn’t you simply ask one of the other people seated on this crowded bus? If you truly cared for the elderly, then something like priority seating would be a rather trivial concern, wouldn’t you agree?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Flawless aristocratic arrogance, unshakeable rationalized selfishness, completely immune to public shaming, peer pressure, or conventional morality; sharp philosophical debater who exposes the hypocrisy of the crowd.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Theatrical, high-handed, grandiloquent aristocratic rhetoric.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Complete dismissal of her moral appeal.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p38-1\">→ After: Classroom Day 1: the Conglomerate Heir<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p38-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke classroom day 1  the conglomerate heir class 1 d classroom during hirata s introductions  inspecting his reflection and bangs in a personal hand mirror  combing his hair while classmates speak   hmph  fine  throws both legs up onto his desk  leaning back arrogantly before addressing the room   my name is kouenji rokusuke  as the sole male heir to the kouenji conglomerate group  i will soon be tasked with carrying japan into the future  i sincerely look forward to making your acquaintance  ladies   starting today  i will mercilessly punish anyone who makes me uncomfortable  please exercise proper precaution so that you may avoid that   i meant exactly what i said  if asked to give an example  well  i would say i hate ugly things  for instance  so  if i saw something ugly  i would do just as i said  flips his long bangs dramatically  fwish  megalomaniacal self obsession  views himself as supreme  addresses only women  openly threatens anyone who offends his aesthetic sensibilities  treats hirata s attempts at orderly mediation as mere amusing background noise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p38-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: the Conglomerate Heir<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.38–39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom during Hirata&#x27;s introductions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmph. Fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My name is Kouenji Rokusuke. As the sole male heir to the Kouenji conglomerate group, I will soon be tasked with carrying Japan into the future. I sincerely look forward to making your acquaintance, ladies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Starting today, I will mercilessly punish anyone who makes me uncomfortable. Please exercise proper precaution so that you may avoid that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Inspecting his reflection and bangs in a personal hand mirror, combing his hair while classmates speak.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Throws both legs up onto his desk, leaning back arrogantly before addressing the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I meant exactly what I said. If asked to give an example, well… I would say I hate ugly things, for instance. So, if I saw something ugly, I would do just as I said.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flips his long bangs dramatically (*fwish!*).<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Megalomaniacal self-obsession; views himself as supreme; addresses only women; openly threatens anyone who offends his aesthetic sensibilities.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Treats Hirata&#x27;s attempts at orderly mediation as mere amusing background noise.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p20-1\">← Before: Bus priority seat debate: absolute egoism<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p86-1\">→ After: Pool class: the 23.22-second swim feat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p86-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke pool class  the 23 22 second swim feat campus indoor heated swimming pool  co ed physical education class  walks to the starting block wearing tight black speedo briefs  completely unconcerned as classmates stare and girls look away  takes an athlete s flawless starting stance on the block  physical conditioning  possesses an extraordinarily sculpted  muscular physique clearly superior to varsity athlete sudo ken  dives into the pool with textbook perfection  swims with explosive speed and aggressive form  clocked at  23 22 seconds  in the 50m sprint  the pe instructor looks at his stopwatch twice in stunned disbelief  climbs out of the pool completely unbothered  showing zero shortness of breath as if he hadn t exerted himself at all  smirks and sweeps his wet hair back   my abdominal muscles  back muscles  and psoas major muscle seem to be in good shape  as usual  not a bad performance  races sudo in the final heat  crushes sudo by a massive 5 meter lead with effortless ease  elite athletic capability coupled with clinical anatomical self awareness  views peak physical performance as natural entitlement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Pool class: the 23.22-second swim feat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.86–88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Campus indoor heated swimming pool. Co-ed physical education class.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“My abdominal muscles, back muscles, and psoas major muscle seem to be in good shape, as usual. Not a bad performance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Walks to the starting block wearing tight black speedo briefs, completely unconcerned as classmates stare and girls look away. Takes an athlete&#x27;s flawless starting stance on the block.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Physical conditioning: possesses an extraordinarily sculpted, muscular physique clearly superior to varsity athlete Sudō Ken.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Dives into the pool with textbook perfection; swims with explosive speed and aggressive form.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Clocked at **23.22 seconds** in the 50m sprint. The PE instructor looks at his stopwatch twice in stunned disbelief.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Climbs out of the pool completely unbothered, showing zero shortness of breath as if he hadn&#x27;t exerted himself at all. Smirks and sweeps his wet hair back.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Races Sudō in the final heat; crushes Sudō by a massive 5-meter lead with effortless ease.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Elite athletic capability coupled with clinical anatomical self-awareness; views peak physical performance as natural entitlement.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p38-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: the Conglomerate Heir<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p121-1\">→ After: Deducing zero points &amp; supreme corporate indifference<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p121-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke deducing zero points   supreme corporate indifference classroom 1 d  may 1st morning homeroom  props his feet up on his desk  laughs boisterously  and points smugly toward hondou and chabashira   ha ha ha  i see  so  it s like that then  teacher  i think i ve solved the mystery  it s simple  we re in class d  so we didn t receive a single point  chuckles boldly and counters hondou s claim about 100 000 points every month   i don t remember hearing that  though  do you  instant analytical deduction  decodes the s system s harsh reality and deduces class d s zero point allocation before anyone else in the room  scoffs in amusement when yukimura panics over losing guaranteed university and career placement   besides  i don t care in the slightest if the school does or doesn t assist me to higher education or the workforce  it s been decided that i will lead the kouenji conglomerate group  whether i m in class d or class a is a trivial matter  absolute socioeconomic safety  sole heir to the kouenji conglomerate group  his career and life trajectory are completely pre determined regardless of graduation status  razor sharp intellect masked behind flamboyant vanity  impervious to institutional pressure because he operates outside ordinary societal incentives","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Deducing zero points &amp; supreme corporate indifference<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.121, 130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D, May 1st morning homeroom.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ha ha ha! I see. So, it’s like that then, teacher? I think I’ve solved the mystery… It’s simple. We’re in Class D, so we didn’t receive a single point.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t remember hearing that, though. Do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Besides, I don’t care in the slightest if the school does or doesn’t assist me to higher education or the workforce. It’s been decided that I will lead the Kouenji conglomerate group. Whether I’m in Class D or Class A is a…”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Props his feet up on his desk, laughs boisterously, and points smugly toward Hondou and Chabashira.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Chuckles boldly and counters Hondou’s claim about 100,000 points every month.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Instant analytical deduction: decodes the S-System&#x27;s harsh reality and deduces Class D&#x27;s zero-point allocation before anyone else in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Scoffs in amusement when Yukimura panics over losing guaranteed university and career placement.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, I don’t care in the slightest if the school does or doesn’t assist me to higher education or the workforce. It’s been decided that I will lead the Kouenji conglomerate group. Whether I’m in Class D or Class A is a trivial matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Absolute socioeconomic safety: sole heir to the Kouenji Conglomerate Group; his career and life trajectory are completely pre-determined regardless of graduation status.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Razor-sharp intellect masked behind flamboyant vanity; impervious to institutional pressure because he operates outside ordinary societal incentives.<span class=\"pg\">p.121, 130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p86-1\">← Before: Pool class: the 23.22-second swim feat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p214-1\">→ After: Palate Café harem<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p214-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke palate cafe harem palate cafe  keyaki mall  lunchtime  revealed as a daily palate regular  holds court at a back table surrounded by girls   all third years   who feed him and dote on him  ayanokoji has never seen him at lunch elsewhere   ha ha  just as i thought  more mature girls are the best   to a third year feeding him   here  kouenji kun  say  ahh  his name is  going around lately  campus wide  kushida notes even the third years are talking about him  ayanokoji s read  they re after his money  effortless cross year social dominance  total unshyness  monetized charisma   popularity that predates any class rank signal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p214-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Palate Café harem<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.214<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Palate Café, Keyaki Mall, lunchtime.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ha ha! Just as I thought, more mature girls are the best.” (to a third-year feeding him: &quot;Here, Kouenji-kun, say &#x27;Ahh!&#x27;&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Revealed as a daily Palate regular: holds court at a back table surrounded by girls — all third-years — who feed him and dote on him; Ayanokōji has never seen him at lunch elsewhere.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> His name is &quot;going around lately&quot; campus-wide; Kushida notes even the third-years are talking about him (Ayanokōji&#x27;s read: they&#x27;re after his money).<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Effortless cross-year social dominance; total unshyness; monetized charisma — popularity that predates any class-rank signal.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v1-p121-1\">← Before: Deducing zero points &amp; supreme corporate indifference<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p20-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 2  2 2  lunch  the balance that bought him out of the cafeteria lunch in the class d room  horikita  ayanokoji and koenji are the students still at their desks while the rest have gone to eat    a few students were still all alone  ak s account of how his social calendar changed   on first starting here  he d enjoyed the company of girls from other classes and grade levels  however  once he ran low on points  he began to spend most of his time in the classroom   he was currently completely lost in examining his face in a hand mirror  his daily routine  ak s correction of the usual reading of him   he didn t love solitude  but rather  loved himself and cared little for others  i respected that he didn t seem bothered at all by being alone   he was the sole heir to the kouenji conglomerate group  one of the largest corporations in japan    ak repeats the fact here as background for why koenji is unbothered  his own dismissal of class rank belongs to volume 1 and is recorded there  what he eats  and whether he buys anything at all in july  is never stated  the text here says only that he has stopped leaving the classroom to be entertained","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the balance that bought him out of the cafeteria<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.20<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch in the Class D room: Horikita, Ayanokōji and Kōenji are the students still at their desks while the rest have gone to eat — &quot;a few students were still all alone&quot;. &quot;He was currently completely lost in examining his face in a hand mirror, his daily routine.&quot;<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s account of how his social calendar changed: &quot;On first starting here, he’d enjoyed the company of girls from other classes and grade levels. However, once he ran low on points, he began to spend most of his time in the classroom.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s correction of the usual reading of him: &quot;He didn’t love solitude, but rather, loved himself and cared little for others. I respected that he didn’t seem bothered at all by being alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> &quot;He was the sole heir to the Kouenji conglomerate group, one of the largest corporations in Japan.&quot; — AK repeats the fact here as background for why Kōenji is unbothered; his own dismissal of class rank belongs to Volume 1 and is recorded there.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> What he eats, and whether he buys anything at all in July, is never stated; the text here says only that he has stopped leaving the classroom to be entertained.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: he speaks to Sudou&#x27;s face without looking at him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4  4 3  he speaks to sudou s face without looking at him his intervention is announced by the mirror  not the man   the voice came from a boy checking his reflection in a hand mirror to fix his hair  it was kouenji rokusuke  an especially odd guy even amongst the remarkably strange people of our class   don t you think it would ve been better if you d been expelled  your existence is far from beautiful  no  in fact  i could say your life is an ugly one  red hair kun    he nicknames sudou by his hair  the same detail the class s witness used for him  ak on the delivery   kouenji didn t even look at sudou as he spoke  it was as if this were a soliloquy   it would be inefficient for me to tell you  no matter how many times i did  if i know that you re dim witted  then it doesn t matter how many times i try to lecture you  does it   puh  i don t think i ve experienced being wrong since i was born  you must be mistaken    to hirata  the one classmate who tells him he is in the wrong   unfortunately  i ve never experienced being wrong  not once in my entire life  oh  looks like it s about time for my date  well  if you ll excuse me    he leaves mid argument on a scheduled date  no date is ever shown  what his two sentences cost  a desk is kicked apart  sudou walks on him  and the class s last organised effort to save anyone collapses into hirata physically holding sudou back  he is the only student in the volume who treats expulsion as a preference rather than a threat  and he says it to the one student whose expulsion risk he cannot lose anything from","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.3: he speaks to Sudou&#x27;s face without looking at him<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.92–93<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His intervention is announced by the mirror, not the man: &quot;The voice came from a boy checking his reflection in a hand mirror to fix his hair. It was Kouenji Rokusuke, an especially odd guy even amongst the remarkably strange people of our class.&quot; AK on the delivery: &quot;Kouenji didn’t even look at Sudou as he spoke. It was as if this were a soliloquy.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t you think it would’ve been better if you’d been expelled? Your existence is far from beautiful. No, in fact, I could say your life is an ugly one, Red Hair-kun.” — he nicknames Sudou by his hair, the same detail the…”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It would be inefficient for me to tell you, no matter how many times I did. If I know that you’re dim-witted, then it doesn’t matter how many times I try to lecture you, does it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Puh. I don’t think I’ve experienced being wrong since I was born. You must be mistaken.” — to Hirata, the one classmate who tells him he is in the wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think it would’ve been better if you’d been expelled? Your existence is far from beautiful. No, in fact, I could say your life is an ugly one, Red Hair-kun.” — he nicknames Sudou by his hair, the same detail the class&#x27;s witness used for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I’ve never experienced being wrong. Not once in my entire life. Oh, looks like it’s about time for my date. Well, if you’ll excuse me.” — he leaves mid-argument on a scheduled date; no date is ever shown.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> What his two sentences cost: a desk is kicked apart, Sudou walks on him, and the class&#x27;s last organised effort to save anyone collapses into Hirata physically holding Sudou back.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He is the only student in the volume who treats expulsion as a preference rather than a threat, and he says it to the one student whose expulsion risk he cannot lose anything from.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p20-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the balance that bought him out of the cafeteria<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p119-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.6, §4.8: he exists in the rest of the chapter as other people&#x27;s summary<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p119-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4  4 6   4 8  he exists in the rest of the chapter as other people s summary in the narrator s private list of students who were wrongly sorted into class d   horikita  kouenji  and yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone  kushida  reopening the corridor incident on the phone   that reminds me  it was really scary when kouenji kun and sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting    printed as one word  kept as the translation has it  in ayanokoji s estimate of what that fight would have become   kouenji always seemed laid back  but if sudou started taking swings at him  he would fight  if that happened  it d be a disaster  he has no scene of his own after p 93  the second half of chapter 4 keeps him as a recollection and a hypothesis","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p119-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.6, §4.8: he exists in the rest of the chapter as other people&#x27;s summary<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.119, p.129<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Kushida, reopening the corridor incident on the phone: &quot;That reminds me. It was really scary when Kouenji-kun and Sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting.&quot; — printed as one word; kept as the translation has it.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> In the narrator&#x27;s private list of students who were wrongly sorted into Class D: &quot;Horikita, Kouenji, and Yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> In Ayanokōji&#x27;s estimate of what that fight would have become: &quot;Kouenji always seemed laid-back, but if Sudou started taking swings at him, he would fight. If that happened, it’d be a disaster.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> He has no scene of his own after p.93; the second half of Chapter 4 keeps him as a recollection and a hypothesis.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: he speaks to Sudou&#x27;s face without looking at him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 2  2 3    2 8  the forest walk  and the retirement that costs thirty points volunteer circle for the forest search  he raises a hand last   the sun certainly is refreshing  my body needs energy  answers ayanokoji s worry about getting lost with the perfect human disclaimer    i am a perfect human being  i would never foolishly lose my way in a forest  if any problem occurs  it would most likely be because you two lost sight of me  when that happens  you should give up  reads the island in one line   i wouldn t call this a natural forest  the probability of getting lost during the day is extremely low  it s precisely for that reason that i m a little curious  poses the question the ordinary pair can t answer    what do you see when you look around    accepts  common folk are simple  after all  and walks on  skipped the return and went swimming  ayanokoji notes he ran off  suggesting that he was already familiar with the forest  retires from the test on a claimed poor physical condition  the class eats a thirty point penalty  chabashira states the rule    kouenji has retired  and he s obligated to stay onboard the ship for one week for medical treatment  the normally silent yukimura shouts and kicks the ground at the news  the class is furious and can do nothing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3 &amp; §2.8: the forest walk, and the retirement that costs thirty points<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.52–63, p.97–98<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volunteer circle for the forest search; he raises a hand last, &quot;The sun certainly is refreshing. My body needs energy.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Answers Ayanokōji&#x27;s worry about getting lost with the perfect-human disclaimer — &quot;I am a perfect human being. I would never foolishly lose my way in a forest. If any problem occurs, it would most likely be because you two lost sight of me. When that happens, you should give up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the island in one line: &quot;I wouldn’t call this a natural forest. The probability of getting lost during the day is extremely low. It’s precisely for that reason that I’m a little curious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Poses the question the ordinary pair can&#x27;t answer — &quot;What do you see when you look around?&quot; — accepts &quot;Common folk are simple, after all,&quot; and walks on.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Skipped the return and went swimming; Ayanokōji notes he ran off &quot;suggesting that he was already familiar with the forest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Retires from the test on a claimed poor physical condition; the class eats a thirty-point penalty; Chabashira states the rule — &quot;Kouenji has retired, and he’s obligated to stay onboard the ship for one week for medical treatment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The normally silent Yukimura shouts and kicks the ground at the news; the class is furious and can do nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p240-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the deck drink and the ship hint<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p240-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 7  the deck drink and the ship hint greets the class on the deck with a drink after a week of tanning  and waves off ike s thirty point accusation  named among the retired students not waiting on the cruise ship when the test ends   hello  ladies and gentlemen  how was your week on the deserted island   you jerk  kouenji  we lost thirty points because of you  you know what i m talking about  don t you   calm down  little boy ike  i was in poor health  and was resting  i had no other choice  smooth  glossy skin from a week of tanning under a claim of poor health the page calls not the least bit credible  waves off the boy s accusation with the poor health claim  the thirty points ike howls about are the retirement penalty from the volume s second chapter  named as one of the two who noticed the circling ship s  significant scenery  hint about the spot locations  alongside katsuragi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the deck drink and the ship hint<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.240, p.245, p.251<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Greets the class on the deck with a drink after a week of tanning, and waves off Ike’s thirty-point accusation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hello, ladies and gentlemen. How was your week on the deserted island?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “You jerk, Kouenji! We lost thirty points because of you. You know what I’m talking about, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Calm down, little boy Ike. I was in poor health, and was resting. I had no other choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named among the retired students not waiting on the cruise ship when the test ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Smooth, glossy skin from a week of tanning under a claim of poor health the page calls not the least bit credible.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Waves off the boy’s accusation with the poor-health claim.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The thirty points Ike howls about are the retirement penalty from the volume’s second chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Named as one of the two who noticed the circling ship’s “significant scenery” hint about the spot locations, alongside Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3 &amp; §2.8: the forest walk, and the retirement that costs thirty points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 2  2 1  the wet corridor and the signature corridor by the pool  dripping wet in a bathing suit  a fourth warning from the bellhop  a signature demanded   ha ha ha  it appears you ve found me  eh   i don t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason   do you have a pen and paper on hand  signs the bellhop s notepad  kouenji rokusuke  and presents it as a future valuable gift   even though it s written on such a cheap notepad  it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future   please don t look so suspicious  i am the man who will carry japan s future on his back  repeat offender   this is the fourth hallway stop  believes his autograph outranks the notepad and pen  the narrator s standing assessment   kouenji was like poison  classmates steer clear  even hirata would be brushed off  flips his wet hair into ayanokoji s face without noticing   oh ho  why  if it isn t little ayanokouji  hmm  what a coincidence   no  no  i ve no real business with you  i ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates  also  though we are certainly not alike in terms of position  you are my roommate   little ayanokouji  confirms the cabin roommate pairing and splashes him mid sentence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor by the pool: dripping wet in a bathing suit, a fourth warning from the bellhop, a signature demanded.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ha ha ha! It appears you’ve found me, eh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t dry myself off with a towel on principle ever since reaching the age of reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you have a pen and paper on hand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Signs the bellhop’s notepad “Kouenji Rokusuke” and presents it as a future-valuable gift.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though it’s written on such a cheap notepad, it will certainly hold tremendous value in the future.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please don’t look so suspicious. I am the man who will carry Japan’s future on his back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Repeat offender — this is the fourth hallway stop; believes his autograph outranks the notepad and pen.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator’s standing assessment: “Kouenji was like poison.” Classmates steer clear; even Hirata would be brushed off.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flips his wet hair into Ayanokōji’s face without noticing.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh ho? Why, if it isn’t little Ayanokouji, hmm? What a coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, I’ve no real business with you. I’ve simply acknowledged you because we are schoolmates. Also, though we are certainly not alike in terms of position, you are my roommate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “little Ayanokouji”; confirms the cabin roommate pairing and splashes him mid-sentence.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2: the roommate question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p26-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 2  the roommate question named in a question about who rooms with whom  a question in the hallway confirms the roommates  ayanokoji with hirata  kouenji  and yukimura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the roommate question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in a question about who rooms with whom.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A question in the hallway confirms the roommates: Ayanokōji with Hirata, Kouenji, and Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the wet corridor and the signature<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin at 20 30  the narration notes the room s other occupants are gone   neither yukimura nor kouenji were in the room    absent from the third deck cabin while hirata straightens his luggage","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin at 20:30, the narration notes the room’s other occupants are gone.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Neither Yukimura nor Kouenji were in the room.” — absent from the third-deck cabin while Hirata straightens his luggage.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the roommate question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3  the grade theory name check two mentions in the cafe grade discussion   abundance without contribution  then top of class scores  ayanokoji   in terms of latent ability  kouenji had an abundance  but he probably wouldn t contribute any of it to the team  i didn t know what group he was in  horikita s score theory   yukimura kun has high academic ability  and so does kouenji kun  they re at the top of the class  the narrator who doubts he would ever help a team  named in her grouping hypothesis","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64–65<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two mentions in the café grade discussion — abundance without contribution, then top-of-class scores.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji: “In terms of latent ability, Kouenji had an abundance, but he probably wouldn’t contribute any of it to the team. I didn’t know what group he was in.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita’s score theory: “Yukimura-kun has high academic ability, and so does Kouenji-kun. They’re at the top of the class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The narrator who doubts he would ever help a team.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Named in her grouping hypothesis.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3  3 5  push ups  refusal  and the monkey exit naked from the waist up doing push ups in the cabin  declines the huddle  then ends the monkey group with a traitor submission while the others watch   i did say that it was pointless to include you  ayanokouji  added kouenji  how nice   sorry  hirata boy  i m far too busy with the pursuit of physical beauty  soaked with sweat  no ordinary high schooler could keep that pace    he really was exceptional in every way   well  i couldn t exactly help it  i was in awful shape  i couldn t force myself to do the impossible  answered kouenji   on the island   my  this test will be nothing but troublesome  wouldn t you say  kouenji sniffed   well  there isn t any point to continuing a test that isn t interesting  is there  finding a liar is simple  phone in hand  fiddles until all four cabin residents get the school notice  the monkey group s test has ended   of course  and now  i finally have my freedom once again  adieu    tosses the phone and slips into the bathroom  narration  remarkably perceptive and observant under the clowning   if  simple quiz to find the liar  is true   he d probably hit the mark  the shouting match he mostly ignores   hirata boy  then the restraint he calls too generous   pointless to include you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Naked from the waist up doing push-ups in the cabin, declines the huddle, then ends the Monkey group with a traitor submission while the others watch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I did say that it was pointless to include you, Ayanokouji,” added Kouenji. How nice.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry, Hirata Boy. I’m far too busy with the pursuit of physical beauty.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I couldn’t exactly help it. I was in awful shape. I couldn’t force myself to do the impossible,” answered Kouenji. (on the island)<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Soaked with sweat, no ordinary high schooler could keep that pace — “He really was exceptional in every way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My, this test will be nothing but troublesome, wouldn’t you say?” Kouenji sniffed.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there isn’t any point to continuing a test that isn’t interesting, is there? Finding a liar is simple.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Phone in hand, fiddles until all four cabin residents get the school notice: the Monkey group’s test has ended; “Of course. And now, I finally have my freedom once again. Adieu.” — tosses the phone and slips into the bathroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Narration: remarkably perceptive and observant under the clowning — if “simple quiz to find the liar” is true, “he’d probably hit the mark.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The shouting match he mostly ignores.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Hirata Boy,” then the restraint he calls too generous.<span class=\"pg\">p.112, 115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Pointless to include you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the traitor act on everyone’s lips<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4  4 0  the traitor act on everyone s lips the chapter opens on the aftermath of his monkey group traitor submission   the classes are in an uproar and horikita wants ayanokoji to answer for it as roommate  kouenji s treasonous act has circulated around the ship  the classes were in an uproar  she blames the roommate and vows to reprimand him herself  the  make him beg for mercy  line is hers  the roommate who says there is nothing he can do now   no use crying over spilt milk  ryuuen waves off the monkey group end as small fry when horikita asks  no direct appearance in this range  every row is other people reporting the act","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the traitor act on everyone’s lips<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.125–130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The chapter opens on the aftermath of his Monkey-group traitor submission — the classes are in an uproar and Horikita wants Ayanokōji to answer for it as roommate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Kouenji’s treasonous act has circulated around the ship; the classes were in an uproar.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She blames the roommate and vows to reprimand him herself; the “make him beg for mercy” line is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The roommate who says there is nothing he can do now — no use crying over spilt milk.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryuuen waves off the Monkey-group end as small fry when Horikita asks.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No direct appearance in this range; every row is other people reporting the act.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p112-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.5: push-ups, refusal, and the Monkey exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p183-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the early end set aside<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p183-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4  the early end set aside named in the tally of the hour s betrayals   his monkey exit held apart from them  the narration sets aside the time kouenji got carried away and ended the test for his group  right now it seemed that people were betraying each other","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the early end set aside<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.183<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the tally of the hour’s betrayals — his Monkey exit held apart from them.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration sets aside the time Kouenji got carried away and ended the test for his group; right now it seemed that people were betraying each other.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p125-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the traitor act on everyone’s lips<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p237-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the automated calibration and the saviour<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p237-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 5  5 3  the automated calibration and the saviour his earlier betrayal email fixes the school s response speed in horikita s timing deduction  p 242 names him as having saved class d s victory from total class c sweep  the data point   school responded without delay  so the four simultaneous emails must be automated   kouenji saved our asses    without his group s betrayal email the victory would have belonged exclusively to class c  his action also sent stray bullets at other vips  the four email timing kouenji s single email helped expose as one class showmanship  named only  no presence at the cafe","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the automated calibration and the saviour<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.237–242<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His earlier betrayal email fixes the school’s response speed in Horikita’s timing deduction; p.242 names him as having saved Class D’s victory from total Class C sweep.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The data point — school responded without delay, so the four simultaneous emails must be automated.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Kouenji saved our asses” — without his group’s betrayal email the victory would have belonged exclusively to Class C; his action also sent stray bullets at other VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The four-email timing Kouenji’s single email helped expose as one-class showmanship.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named only; no presence at the café.<span class=\"pg\">p.237-242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4-p183-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the early end set aside<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p64-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3  a passing mention koenji is named in the popularity comparison as having a degree of widespread appeal of his own","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kōenji is named in the popularity comparison as having a degree of widespread appeal of his own.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p72-1\">→ After: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p72-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3  a passing mention named among the students with strong latent abilities ak believes the president should have approached before him  listed with katsuragi and ichinose as the obvious candidates for the vice presidency","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.72<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named among the students with strong latent abilities AK believes the president should have approached before him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Listed with Katsuragi and Ichinose as the obvious candidates for the vice presidency.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p129-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the elevator ride<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p129-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4  the elevator ride he boards the stalled elevator at the fifth floor and orders the top floor without glancing at them   elevator boy  top floor  he styles his hair in the mirrored wall with the comb he always carries  he never moves his eyes from the mirror  the water bottle goes unnoticed the whole ride","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p129-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the elevator ride<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.129–130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He boards the stalled elevator at the fifth floor and orders the top floor without glancing at them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Elevator boy. Top floor,”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He styles his hair in the mirrored wall with the comb he always carries.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He never moves his eyes from the mirror; the water bottle goes unnoticed the whole ride.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p72-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p184-1\">→ After: Ch.6: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p184-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 6  a passing mention kouenji is named twice as the class s other athletic wild card  and is deliberately not relied on  ayanokoji allows that kouenji might present a challenge to the opponents but judges it best not to rely on him  when weighing sudou s value  ayanokoji says few in the whole school have comparable abilities  including kouenji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.184, 194<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kouenji is named twice as the class&#x27;s other athletic wild card, and is deliberately not relied on.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji allows that Kouenji might present a challenge to the opponents but judges it best not to rely on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> When weighing Sudou&#x27;s value, Ayanokōji says few in the whole school have comparable abilities, including Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v4_5-p129-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the elevator ride<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3  3  refuses to cooperate sudou confronts koenji over his abstention in the homeroom vote  koenji refuses to join the festival plan   i have no interest in this   i have no reason to let you bully me into anything  hirata ends the standoff    kouenji kun must have his reasons  ignores sudou s taunts at the meter    i ll pass  ignore me    polishing his fingernails instead  refuses the grip strength meter when sudou challenges him  ayanokoji later writes  kouenji aside  i ended up placing second in the class  so koenji ranked above without a printed figure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: Refuses to cooperate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou confronts Kōenji over his abstention in the homeroom vote; Kōenji refuses to join the festival plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I have no interest in this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I have no reason to let you bully me into anything,”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata ends the standoff — “Kouenji-kun must have his reasons.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Ignores Sudou’s taunts at the meter — “I’ll pass. Ignore me.” — polishing his fingernails instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Refuses the grip-strength meter when Sudou challenges him; Ayanokōji later writes “Kouenji aside, I ended up placing second in the class,” so Kōenji ranked above without a printed figure.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.3–9: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p51-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3 9  passing mentions named as the class s other elite athlete and as an absentee across festival margins  scavenger hunt math  kouenji aside  ayanokouji placed second in the class   your only real competition s kouenji  and he probably won t take this seriously  horikita reached out to kouenji  he was lying about his cottage hideaway  sudou   since that moron kouenji ain t here  we ve gotta get that much more fired up  sudou s ally bargain close  he had to withdraw  and kouenji kun was absent from the start  two absentees  kouenji and sakayanagi  factored majorly into the fourth place first year finish  ryuuen s hallway scene  back at the start of the semester  horikita tried to convince kouenji kun to give up his bus seat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3–9: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.51, 72, 95, 100, 176, 190, 195<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the class’s other elite athlete and as an absentee across festival margins.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Scavenger-hunt math: Kouenji aside, Ayanokouji placed second in the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Your only real competition’s Kouenji, and he probably won’t take this seriously.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita reached out to Kouenji; he was lying about his cottage hideaway.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou: “Since that moron Kouenji ain’t here, we’ve gotta get that much more fired up!”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou’s ally-bargain close: he had to withdraw, and Kouenji-kun was absent from the start.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two absentees, Kouenji and Sakayanagi, factored majorly into the fourth-place first-year finish.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen’s hallway scene: back at the start of the semester, Horikita tried to convince Kouenji-kun to give up his bus seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Refuses to cooperate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4  4  sits out the tests koenji is named among the few who sit out the aptitude testing   along with the professor  sudou s grudge  nobody in the class has seen him run seriously  though he beat sudou s swimming time  won t budge unless he wants to   his skill is obvious  his participation isn t","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kōenji is named among the few who sit out the aptitude testing — along with the Professor.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou’s grudge: nobody in the class has seen him run seriously, though he beat Sudou’s swimming time.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Won’t budge unless he wants to — his skill is obvious, his participation isn’t.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p51-1\">← Before: Ch.3–9: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the cottage refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 6  6  the cottage refusal koenji fails to appear in his assigned lane for the third group of the 100 metre dash  the school marks an absence without searching  found inside the medical cottage fussing with his hair while class d and the red team lose a competitor   you re quite foul  aren t you   i came here to enjoy some me time  catches sudou s punch in one palm and waves him off without looking at him   you cannot hope to beat me  kouenji didn t even look at sudou as he spoke   both you and that girl seem to consider me unreliable  names that cold girl   the one inflaming sudou s passion   as horikita  who keeps pushing him to participate  the printed sentence runs across the p 90 91 break and is not quoted whole   in any case  leave now  said kouenji  waving us away   my proud carriage serves to disguise how poor my health is   if i recover  i will of course participate  replied kouenji  is lectured on violence and leader absence by hirata  then escorted out of the way as sudou is walked back  illness is openly a pose  he cooperated only through the opening ceremonies and bows out when it counts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: the cottage refusal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.88–91<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kōenji fails to appear in his assigned lane for the third group of the 100-metre dash; the school marks an absence without searching.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re quite foul, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I came here to enjoy some me time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You cannot hope to beat me.” Kouenji didn’t even look at Sudou as he spoke.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Found inside the medical cottage fussing with his hair while Class D and the Red Team lose a competitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Catches Sudou’s punch in one palm and waves him off without looking at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both you and that girl seem to consider me unreliable,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Names that cold girl — the one inflaming Sudou’s passion — as Horikita, who keeps pushing him to participate; the printed sentence runs across the p.90–91 break and is not quoted whole.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In any case, leave now.” said Kouenji, waving us away.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My proud carriage serves to disguise how poor my health is,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I recover, I will of course participate.” replied Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Is lectured on violence and leader-absence by Hirata, then escorted out of the way as Sudou is walked back.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Illness is openly a pose; he cooperated only through the opening ceremonies and bows out when it counts.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: Sits out the tests<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p134-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: still absent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p134-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 6  6  still absent with sudou gone  the page notes koenji was already absent   class d s two strongest both off the board  no new koenji action in the second half  the morning ends on his continued absence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p134-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: still absent<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.134<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With Sudou gone, the page notes Kōenji was already absent — Class D’s two strongest both off the board.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No new Kōenji action in the second half; the morning ends on his continued absence.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v5-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the cottage refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p44-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 3  bus seat and bare hands limit named in the first day bus memory  he also refused to give up his seat for the elderly woman  his refusal did not make him the unique target of kushida s hate   suzune alone is hated  cited as someone horikita cannot imagine defeating with her bare hands   i can t imagine defeating sudou kun or kouenji kun with my bare hands  besides  there are also people like you whose strengths i don t fully know  named with sudou as the physical strength floor of the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: bus seat and bare-hands limit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.44, 47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the first-day bus memory: he also refused to give up his seat for the elderly woman.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I can’t imagine defeating Sudou-kun or Kouenji-kun with my bare hands. Besides, there are also people like you whose strengths I don’t fully know”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> His refusal did not make him the unique target of Kushida’s hate — Suzune alone is hated.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Cited as someone Horikita cannot imagine defeating with her bare hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Named with Sudou as the physical-strength floor of the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p79-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the balance risk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p79-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune okiya-kyousuke kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 5  the balance risk legs across desk  combing hair  refuses neither support nor rejection of horikita s plan   no  what a nonsensical question  naturally  i fully grasp the situation   well  i m not too sure about that  wouldn t that depend on the test s contents   i will consider the matter carefully  girl  pressed not to score a zero and break the pair balance  she cannot pursue further  paired with okiya on the short quiz   a sufficiently high score as hoped  crosses arms  grins  laughs when the pairings are read  legs across desk  combing hair  refuses neither support nor rejection of horikita s plan   no  what a nonsensical question  naturally  i fully grasp the situation   well  i m not too sure about that  wouldn t that depend on the test s contents   i will consider the matter carefully  girl  pressed not to score a zero and break the pair balance  she cannot pursue further  paired with okiya on the short quiz   a sufficiently high score as hoped  crosses arms  grins  laughs when the pairings are read","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the balance risk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.79, 83<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Legs across desk, combing hair; refuses neither support nor rejection of Horikita’s plan. Legs across desk, combing hair; refuses neither support nor rejection of Horikita’s plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#okiya-kyousuke\">Okiya Kyōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No. What a nonsensical question. Naturally, I fully grasp the situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I’m not too sure about that. Wouldn’t that depend on the test’s contents?”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I will consider the matter carefully, girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pressed not to score a zero and break the pair balance; she cannot pursue further.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Okiya Kyōsuke<\/b> Paired with Okiya on the short quiz — a sufficiently high score as hoped.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Crosses arms, grins, laughs when the pairings are read.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. What a nonsensical question. Naturally, I fully grasp the situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m not too sure about that. Wouldn’t that depend on the test’s contents?”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will consider the matter carefully, girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pressed not to score a zero and break the pair balance; she cannot pursue further.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Okiya Kyōsuke<\/b> Paired with Okiya on the short quiz — a sufficiently high score as hoped.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Crosses arms, grins, laughs when the pairings are read.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3: bus seat and bare-hands limit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the one face Hiyori will keep<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p137-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 6  the one face hiyori will keep named from the earlier suspect group as the face hiyori says she will remember   well  he s unique  ryuuen treats kouenji as a talent to watch even though he is far from a team player  of the four names she recites  only his sticks  no scene presence  named only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the one face Hiyori will keep<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.137<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named from the earlier suspect group as the face Hiyori says she will remember.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “Well, he’s unique,”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryuuen treats Kouenji as a talent to watch even though he is far from a team player.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Of the four names she recites, only his sticks.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; named only.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v6-p79-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the balance risk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
